---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// This page explains the editorial access pathways and provides direct access links.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Newsroom Desk — Nick’s Media"
  description="Secure access portal for Nick’s Media editors, journalists, and producers."
  noindex
>
  <article class="legal section-pad" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding-top: 60px;">
    <div class="section-label">
      <span>Newsroom</span> Editorial Access Portal
    </div>
    <h1>Editorial Workspace &amp; <em>Content Desk.</em></h1>
    <p class="legal-intro">
      Welcome to the Nick’s Media newsroom publishing desk. Our editorial space is powered by Sanity Studio, where our reporters, editors, and producers draft, review, preview, and publish stories and video content.
    </p>

    <!-- Hero Access Box -->
    <div class="portal-card">
      <span style="font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #f6b6b7; font-weight: 700; display: block; margin-bottom: 12px;">DIRECT STUDIO ACCESS</span>
      <h2 style="color: #fff; font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 12px; font-family: var(--serif);">Open Editorial Newsroom Studio</h2>
      <p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 24px; max-width: 620px;">
        Sign in to create, edit, or publish breaking news, investigative reporting, and video packages. Authenticate with your assigned newsroom credentials for project <code>cgcw2i33</code>.
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <a
          href="https://manage.sanity.io/projects/cgcw2i33"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button button-light"
          style="background: var(--red); color: #fff; border-color: var(--red); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1px;"
        >
          Open Cloud Studio Desk ↗
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://manage.sanity.io/projects/cgcw2i33/team"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button button-light"
          style="background: transparent; color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1px;"
        >
          Manage Editorial Team &amp; Roles ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial Roles Grid -->
    <section>
      <h2>Editorial Roles &amp; Permissions</h2>
      <p>
        For enterprise production media security, user authentication is managed via Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Passwords are never stored in plaintext or exposed client-side.
      </p>
      <div class="portal-grid">
        <div class="portal-tile">
          <span style="font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--red); letter-spacing: 1.2px; text-transform: uppercase;">Leadership</span>
          <h3>Administrator</h3>
          <p>Full control over editorial schemas, desk configurations, dataset backups, API tokens, and user credentials.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="portal-tile">
          <span style="font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--red); letter-spacing: 1.2px; text-transform: uppercase;">Publishing</span>
          <h3>Senior Editor</h3>
          <p>Can draft, edit, review reporter submissions, and publish stories and video content live to the global audience.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="portal-tile">
          <span style="font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--red); letter-spacing: 1.2px; text-transform: uppercase;">Field &amp; Desk</span>
          <h3>Reporter / Contributor</h3>
          <p>Draft stories, file leads, upload footage, and submit for editorial verification before publication.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Team Credentials Guide -->
    <section style="margin-top: 36px;">
      <h2>Inviting Team Members (3–4 Logins)</h2>
      <p>
        To grant credentials to your editorial staff:
      </p>
      <ol style="line-height: 1.8; color: #4b5563; font-size: 15px; padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Go to <strong><a href="https://manage.sanity.io/projects/cgcw2i33/team" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--red); text-decoration: underline;">Sanity Project Team Settings</a></strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>"Invite members"</strong>.</li>
        <li>Enter the editor's email address and assign their role (e.g. <em>Editor</em> or <em>Administrator</em>).</li>
        <li>They will receive a secure single-sign-on invitation email to set their login credentials.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Local / Dedicated Studio Hosting -->
    <section style="margin-top: 36px;">
      <h2>Local / Dedicated Studio Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The Studio codebase is also available in this repository under <code>/studio</code>. You can run it locally with:
      </p>
      <pre style="background: #0b192c; color: #f8fafc; padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; border-left: 4px solid var(--red);"><code>cd studio
npm run dev</code></pre>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">
        It opens at <code>http://localhost:3333</code> where team members can log in directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="legal-actions" style="margin-top: 48px;">
      <a class="button button-dark" href="/">Back to the newsroom ↗</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
